# Testing

Write unit tests with [gest](https://github.com/lordnynex/gest). Keep a standard `TestXxx(*testing.T)` entry that calls `gest.Run`. Do not add other assertion libraries. Do not use `cmp.Diff` or `t.Fatal("wrong")` style checks.

- Structure suites with `Describe` / `Context` / `When` / `It`. Use `DescribeTable` for table cases.
- Assert with `t.Expect` / `t.Require` and gest matchers (`Equal`, `BeNil`, `Contain`).
- Use `t.Parallel()` when tests do not share mutable state.
- Use `t.Context()` for cancelable work. Put fixtures in `testdata/`.
- Cover exported behavior, including error paths.

```go
// ❌ BAD
func TestNew(t *testing.T) {
    if New() == nil {
        t.Fatal("wrong")
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD
func TestNew(t *testing.T) {
    gest.Run(t, "New", func(s *gest.S) {
        s.It("returns a server", func(t *gest.T) {
            t.Expect(New()).NotTo(gest.BeNil())
        })
    })
}
```
